## 4️⃣ DATABASE DESIGN (SUPABASE POSTGRES)

### 🗄️ Schema Specification

#### 1. `users` (Synced Profiles)
| Column | Type | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `id` | UUID (PK) | Matches Clerk User ID. |
| `email` | Text | Primary email (Unique). |
| `full_name` | Text | Display name. |
| `plan` | Text | 'free', 'pro', 'plus'. Default 'free'. |
| `created_at` | Timestamptz | Signup date. |

**RLS Policy**:
-   `SELECT`: Users can see themsevles. Service Role sees all.
-   `UPDATE`: Users can update `full_name`. Only webhook updates `plan`.

#### 2. `github_identities` (Secure Token Storage)
| Column | Type | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `user_id` | UUID (PK, FK) | Link to `users`. |
| `github_id` | Text | GitHub numeric ID. |
| `username` | Text | GitHub handle. |
| `access_token` | Text (Encrypted) | OAuth token for API calls. |

**RLS Policy**:
-   `SELECT`: User can see own.
-   `INSERT/UPDATE`: Only via Server-Side functions (never client).

#### 3. `scans` (Analysis Jobs)
| Column | Type | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `id` | UUID (PK) | . |
| `user_id` | UUID (FK) | Owner. Nullable for Guests. |
| `repo_owner` | Text | . |
| `repo_name` | Text | . |
| `status` | Text | 'queued', 'processing', 'completed', 'failed'. |
| `result_summary`| JSONB | Light summary for list view. |
| `created_at` | Timestamptz | . |

**RLS Policy**:
-   `INSERT`: Authenticated users.
-   `SELECT`: User can see own scans.
-   `UPDATE`: Only Service Role (Worker) can update status.

#### 4. `scan_snapshots` (Heavy Data)
| Column | Type | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `scan_id` | UUID (PK, FK) | Link to `scans`. |
| `b_full_analysis` | JSONB | The massive AI output. |
| `raw_file_tree` | JSONB | Cached file structure. |

**RLS Policy**:
-   `SELECT`: User can see own.

#### 5. `usage_meters` (Rate Limits)
| Column | Type | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `user_id` | UUID (PK, FK) | . |
| `period_day` | Date | YYYY-MM-DD. |
| `scan_count` | Int | Default 0. |
| `deep_count` | Int | Default 0. |

**RLS Policy**:
-   `SELECT`: User can see own usage.
-   `UPDATE`: Only Service Role (Worker) can increment.

